description:
Filed by the governor at 16:50Z on 2026-11-03. This is the VS Code twin that task-ac587df5 (JetBrains, DONE as d5f36e82) marked out of scope. JetBrains went first, and this row brings VS Code to parity. Citations checked at 8a53505e.

PROBLEM. VS Code's Task Detail "Prior hand-offs" cards build their title from fields the daemon never writes, so every title reads just "#1", "#2" and so on. The releaser, the release time and the reason are lost. The test fixture encodes the same wrong shape, so the suite stays green.

EVIDENCE (HEAD 8a53505e).
- **Daemon:** packages/moe-daemon/src/types/schema.ts:553-571, HandoffNote {whatIsDone, whatRemains, pitfalls?, openQuestions?, releasedBy?, releasedAt, reason?, diskState?}, written by tools/releaseTask.ts.
- **VS Code:**
  - moe-vscode/src/types/moe.ts:202-210: HandoffNote {from?, to?, createdAt?, ...};
  - moe-vscode/src/panels/TaskDetailPanel.ts:1310-1314: renderHandoff's title reads h.from, h.to and h.createdAt;
  - moe-vscode/tests/task-time-budget.test.cjs:224: the richTask fixture uses from/to/createdAt.
- **Same bug and repro as the JetBrains row:** /mnt/d/moe-scratch/hunt-2597/B/zzHunt2597B.wire.test.ts F3. A real release_task writes the handoff keys `reason, releasedAt, releasedBy, whatIsDone, whatRemains`.

FIX DIRECTION. Mirror the landed JetBrains header exactly (d5f36e82, TaskDetailDialog.kt:917-925):
- "#N";
- then " released by <releasedBy>" when it is set;
- then " (<releasedAt>)" when set;
- then ": <reason>" when set.
Every value stays HTML-escaped as today. Update the HandoffNote type to the daemon's fields, and fix the fixture to the daemon's shape. Add a test that fails if the title reads from/to/createdAt again, and one showing a note without the new fields still renders "#N".

SCOPE. moe-vscode only, with no JetBrains or daemon change. Gates: moe-vscode `npm test` and `npm run compile`, run in the task worktree.

